ScrollTemplates.xml

# ══ THE PANEL TEMPLATE KIT — the reference's own, off the player's chain (1751, window 31) ══
# TWO entries, because the reference splits this kit the way it splits every other: the `.lua`
# carries the verbs and the `.xml` the templates. Listing the `.xml` alone brings none of the verbs
# (`every_chain_xml_brings_its_own_lua` is a gate because that already bit twice).
#
# ONE swap, THREE of our files, which is why it had to move as a unit and why 1837 measured it
# before anyone executed it:
#   * `UIPanelTemplates.xml` — DELETED. Our 18 templates were a strict SUBSET of the reference's,
#     zero benilla-only additions, so the template half is a pure gain.
#   * the scroll half of `ScrollTemplates.xml` — `FauxScrollFrameTemplate`, `FauxScrollFrame_*`,
#     `ScrollFrame_*` — now the chain's. What stays there is `BenillaScrollBarTemplate` and
#     `BenillaScrollTroughTemplate`, which are ours and which six windows still inherit.
#   * the `PanelTemplates_*` family out of `UiPanels.xml`.
#
# It could not be split: `ScrollTemplates.xml` sits ABOVE this entry, so the chain's
# `FauxScrollFrameTemplate` lands after ours and wins (registration is last-in). There is no
# ordering that takes the templates without also taking Faux.
#
# GAINED: `TabButtonTemplate`, and the whole `ScrollingEdit_*` family, which we had NOWHERE — that
# is HelpFrame's named blocker, answered as a side effect. And it unblocks MacroFrame (1835).
Interface\FrameXML\UIPanelTemplates.lua

Interface\FrameXML\UIPanelTemplates.xml
